>&1 | tail -2; diff /tmp/outline2.md story-wiki/Outline.md; cd story-wiki && git log --format='%h %s' | head -5"]], "output": "```console\n1c1\n< # Outline (rev 2) — one SHAP run per instance: when is it a reliable basis for the conclusion?\n---\n> # Outline (rev 3) — one SHAP run per instance: when is it a reliable basis for the conclusion?\n39c39,41\n< ## 4. Paper structure and what each part says (to be sized by `venue`)\n---\n> ## 4. Paper structure and what each part says\n> **Venue (from `venue-repo`'s record):** NeurIPS 2026 main track, single column, **≤ 9 pages for everything in the body including figures and tables**; references, appendix and the 16-item checklist do not count; submission mode (anonymous). Contribution type **General** (empirical evaluation): the paper is *not* framed as a Negative Results paper even if the answer is \"unreliable\"; its contribution is the protocol and the map of conditions, and R1 may fail inside it. Page budget (venue's recommendation, adopted): abstract + intro ≈ 1.3 p; related work ≈ 0.6; setting/protocol ≈ 1.4; design ≈ 1 (with Table 1); results ≈ 3.7; discussion/limits ≈ 0.7. **Page count decides cuts, from `paper-repo`'s compiled build, in the order of §5.** The headline's scope sentence (B=50 random rows, these datasets and models) belongs in the abstract and §4, not only in appendix A2.\n> \n46c48\n< | 4 Experimental design | Datasets (German Credit, ACS-Employment, ACS-Income, Pima, GMSC), models (LR/RF/GBM/MLP, accuracy), budgets, n, R, seeds, statistics (per-dataset display, per-instance CP intervals, instances as resampling unit, no dataset-level CI). Compute budget. | Pre-registered choices; what was cut and why. |\n---\n> | 4 Experimental design | **How the experiments are run (from `analysis`'s commitment):** for each instance, model and background the exact value-function table over all 2^d coalitions is computed once; every sampler, including the unchanged `shap` `KernelExplainer` (via a lookup model), draws exactly the coalitions/permutations it would draw against the model, and reads values from the table, so the explainer's randomness is the library's and the exact reference is the solution on the same table. The paper states this, and the validity checks (lookup vs direct evaluation, E1 vs TreeSHAP, LR zero variance). Datasets (German Credit, ACS-Employment, ACS-Income, Pima, GMSC), models (LR/RF/GBM/MLP, accuracy), budgets, n, R, seeds, statistics (per-dataset display, per-instance CP intervals, instances as resampling unit, no dataset-level CI). Compute budget. | Pre-registered choices; what was cut and why. |\n89a92\n> - rev 3: venue fixed (NeurIPS 2026, General track, 9 pages incl. figures); page budget and cut-by-compiled-count rule; cached value-table design stated in §4 (analysis); Brief rev 4 (hedged absence claims, H3 as inverse squared margin) matches rev 2's M5 — no change to claims. Figure/table numbering matches `figtab-repo`'s data contract.\n96b4ee5 Outline rev 3: venue, page budget, run design\n9ee6934 Outline rev 2: review #3 adopted\n56f3c0a Outline rev 1: story, claims, experiments, figures\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "967151ac-b0d9-56ab-a408-5117a56e1f83", "at": 1795628207.0520606, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14093, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0eafca44ceb7f39d635808222ed0b241", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "6d667cc9-3fa7-586f-bd22-3783e77d9e04", "at": 1795628207.061903, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14094, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0eafca44ceb7f39d635808222ed0b241", "trust": "agent-repo