s only the venue facts and the cached value-table run design. It leaves the claims M1–M6 and R1 unchanged, and I found nothing to object to in either. I'm sending no message.\n\n- **Venue facts:** these are NeurIPS 2026, General track, 9 body pages, a page budget, and a rule that cuts follow the compiled page count in the order of §5. They fit the plan I reviewed earlier.\n- **Run design:** the design computes the exact value table once and lets the unchanged `shap` explainer read from it. That keeps the explainer's randomness the library's, and it lowers the compute risk I flagged. The validity checks it names (lookup against direct evaluation, E1 against TreeSHAP, the LR zero-variance control) are the right ones.\n\nOnly `analysis` can settle whether the table fits the ~24 CPU-hour budget for the largest d, so the plan should treat it as a point to re-time. I'll re-review if the Brief or Outline changes materially."}}, {"id": "10c6d768-8e8a-5c43-82d2-d3a1b64382e7", "at": 1795628220.189055, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14416, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0eafca44ceb7f39d635808222ed0b241", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "1f8967d9-fca8-5f2e-8d0f-245e2d05f783", "at": 1795628220.3518982, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14418, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0eafca44ceb7f39d635808222ed0b241", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "2a6e0e38-1aff-57f1-9e0a-2a34460dd0ed", "at": 1795628220.3569028, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14419, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "sess